00:03:08.432 --> 00:03:10.567
Because she's our daughter.


00:03:14.634 --> 00:03:16.800
"The whole world is watching."


00:03:18.001 --> 00:03:19.599
That's what they were chanting.


00:03:32.001 --> 00:03:37.001
<i>WCHA, Chicago.</i>


00:03:38.699 --> 00:03:39.766
I'll, uh...


00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:47.567
Okay.
All right, watch your step.


00:03:48.901 --> 00:03:50.466
- Thank you.
- Do me a favor.


00:03:51.033 --> 00:03:53.067
- Don't be long.
- I'll be quick.


00:03:59.001 --> 00:03:59.800
I love you.


00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:01.400
<i>- What's that?
- It's an egg.</i>


00:04:01.432 --> 00:04:04.634
<i>A square egg?</i>


00:04:04.667 --> 00:04:07.200
<i>One of the girls
must have a square egg wig.</i>


00:04:07.234 --> 00:04:10.734
I don't get it.


00:04:11.367 --> 00:04:13.500
Maybe you have to be
drunk to get it.


00:04:13.532 --> 00:04:14.599
It's really funny, Mom.


00:04:14.634 --> 00:04:16.033
These rich people from New York


00:04:16.067 --> 00:04:18.100
move to this
broken-down farmhouse.


00:04:18.134 --> 00:04:20.733
The wife is from a made-up
country and talks really funny.


00:04:20.766 --> 00:04:22.100
Hungary is not
a made-up country.


00:04:22.134 --> 00:04:23.699
Oh, thank God you know that.


00:04:23.733 --> 00:04:25.067
And her hair is beautiful.


00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:27.000
You have fun tonight?


00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:31.067
Mm.
Small talk with lawyers' wives.


00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:32.167
Hotel food.


00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:35.667
Endured a cha-cha
with the senior partner.


00:04:35.699 --> 00:04:37.733
- Yippie demonstration.
- Huh?


00:04:38.201 --> 00:04:41.000
It was... It's a lot of...


00:04:41.033 --> 00:04:44.500
It was like a...
You could, like, feel...


00:04:46.033 --> 00:04:49.634
a shifting current there.


00:04:49.667 --> 00:04:52.100
The cops are
as young as the Yippies.


00:04:55.134 --> 00:04:56.667
All right, slowpoke. Come on.


00:04:56.699 --> 00:04:58.134
- Oh, Mom.
- It's time.


00:04:58.667 --> 00:05:01.666
Erin will fill you in
in the morning.


00:05:02.567 --> 00:05:03.733
Mm-hmm.


00:05:03.766 --> 00:05:05.567
Thank you for
keeping her indoors.


00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:10.134
- Good night, Erin.
- Night.


00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:35.466
You okay?


00:05:36.067 --> 00:05:37.067
Joy?


00:05:41.966 --> 00:05:43.100
Again?


00:05:44.699 --> 00:05:46.033
Should you see the doctor?


00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:48.466
I see him again next week.


00:05:52.699 --> 00:05:54.966
Can you rub my feet?


00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:01.166
My ankles are as big as Dumbo's.


00:06:01.201 --> 00:06:04.166
- No, they're not.
- Oh, my God.


00:06:04.201 --> 00:06:05.634
Just raise it.


00:06:06.432 --> 00:06:09.966
You okay to look at
the Kramer brief for me?


00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:11.666
Best editor I ever had.


00:06:12.966 --> 00:06:15.000
- In college.
- Ever.


00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:20.466
Yes, of course, but...


00:06:22.466 --> 00:06:23.800
can it wait?


00:06:26.167 --> 00:06:27.934
There's something
that can't wait.


00:06:33.533 --> 00:06:35.667
Come here.


00:06:35.699 --> 00:06:38.134
You should become
partner more often.


00:06:38.167 --> 00:06:40.000
Come here.
Talk to you about something.


00:06:40.033 --> 00:06:41.667
Oh, yeah.


00:06:47.067 --> 00:06:49.167
- Oh, honey?
- Yeah?


00:06:49.201 --> 00:06:53.466
Just... the baby.


00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:55.201
It's okay.
Doctor said it was fine.


00:06:55.233 --> 00:07:01.000
No, I know. It's that... I just...
I feel... I feel huge.


00:07:05.634 --> 00:07:07.699
- All right.
- I'm sorry.


00:07:07.733 --> 00:07:10.466
No, don't be sorry.
Don't be sorry.


00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:12.867
Mm, you know,
it's just that I don't...


00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:23.134
I guess I could be convinced
to do something else.


00:07:24.867 --> 00:07:25.901
What's that?


00:07:28.033 --> 00:07:30.100
When you have a big brain...


00:07:31.233 --> 00:07:34.466
- Ah.
- ...why don't you use it?


00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:37.600
Oh, I... I think I have an idea.


00:07:37.634 --> 00:07:38.933
- It's just that...
- Oh, you do?


00:07:38.966 --> 00:07:41.634
Yeah. Yeah.


00:07:45.067 --> 00:07:46.933
- You let me know.
- Okay.


00:07:46.966 --> 00:07:48.600
So far, I like the idea.


00:08:08.134 --> 00:08:10.699
Oh, go easy
while I'm on the job.


00:08:10.733 --> 00:08:12.800
It's not a job
if you're not getting paid.


00:08:14.567 --> 00:08:15.800
Is that any good?


00:08:16.268 --> 00:08:17.901
I wanted to read it
when it came out,


00:08:17.934 --> 00:08:20.100
and then, you know, life.


00:08:20.432 --> 00:08:22.800
Hmm, I don't know.


00:08:23.567 --> 00:08:25.067
Woman cracking up.


00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:28.699
- No love, nowhere.
- Group therapy.


00:08:29.268 --> 00:08:31.500
It's a Christmas gift
from Roy's mother.


00:08:31.533 --> 00:08:32.533
Right?


00:08:32.799 --> 00:08:35.466
I mean, your own mother-in-law
giving you a book like this?


00:08:51.634 --> 00:08:52.700
What is it?


00:08:54.799 --> 00:08:55.799
Beats me.


00:08:56.834 --> 00:08:58.033
Doctor's orders.


00:08:59.167 --> 00:09:00.799
For when I feel, um...


00:09:02.201 --> 00:09:03.667
nothing.


00:09:04.700 --> 00:09:06.500
Hmm, I better not.


00:09:08.201 --> 00:09:09.500
When Roy died,


00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:11.900
people started
looking at me funny.


00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:16.000
Cocked their heads,
you know, in the way people do


00:09:16.033 --> 00:09:18.167
when they can't
look you in the eye.


00:09:18.201 --> 00:09:20.466
Or the way people do
when they think


00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:23.567
you might swan dive off
the Wabash Avenue Bridge.


00:09:27.167 --> 00:09:30.567
"Oh, Lana..."
is all anyone could manage.


00:09:32.466 --> 00:09:33.866
An incomplete thought.


00:09:35.799 --> 00:09:36.834
That's me.


00:09:42.134 --> 00:09:44.432
Those swan dives.


00:09:54.866 --> 00:09:56.567
- Mrs. Griffin?
- Hmm?


00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:58.567
Did you go blonde
for Mr. Griffin?


00:09:58.600 --> 00:10:01.033
No, but I'm sure it didn't hurt.


00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:03.833
Erin and I are gonna do it.


00:10:04.767 --> 00:10:06.600
Your hair is beautiful.


00:10:06.634 --> 00:10:08.799
Blonde is so much prettier
and cleaner.


00:10:08.833 --> 00:10:10.134
My hair looks like dirt.


00:10:10.734 --> 00:10:12.700
She won't even let me
get my ears pierced.


00:10:12.734 --> 00:10:15.734
I don't want you giving
the impression to people


00:10:15.767 --> 00:10:17.466
that you're... fast.


00:10:17.933 --> 00:10:19.567
- She's a woman now.
- Hey.


00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:21.432
And women make their
own decisions, Mrs. Griffin.


00:10:21.466 --> 00:10:22.567
- Shut up.
- Right?


00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:23.667
Charlotte.


00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:29.000
- You got your period?
- Jesus Christ. Stop it.


00:10:29.033 --> 00:10:32.900
Honey!
Why didn't you say something?


00:10:32.933 --> 00:10:34.834
That's embarrassing. No, stop.


00:10:34.866 --> 00:10:36.634
You know it happens to everyone.


00:10:36.667 --> 00:10:39.600
No, I just don't want to talk
about it. Stop. Stop. Shut up.


00:10:39.634 --> 00:10:40.966
Did you find the supplies?


00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:42.500
Oh my God.


00:10:42.533 --> 00:10:44.466
Erin, I'm sure you knew
everything there was to know


00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:45.634
when you got yours.


00:10:51.167 --> 00:10:53.600
I'm sorry, Erin.
That was very rude.


00:10:53.634 --> 00:10:55.067
I had to figure it out
on my own.


00:10:55.700 --> 00:10:58.500
My dad had just died on us.


00:10:58.533 --> 00:11:00.466
- And then my mom, she...
- No, I know, honey.


00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:02.100
I'm... I'm sorry.
I really am sorry.


00:11:05.067 --> 00:11:07.600
All right, you put the casserole
on the table


00:11:07.634 --> 00:11:09.466
and grab the green beans
for me, Erin.


00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:12.432
Something smells good
in here. Hello?


00:11:13.167 --> 00:11:14.167
Hello!


00:11:15.833 --> 00:11:18.100
- Okay, that's...
- Can we say Grace tonight?


00:11:19.134 --> 00:11:20.933
Oh, we only do that when...


00:11:20.966 --> 00:11:23.600
- On certain occasions...
- I'd like to tonight. For Erin.


00:11:25.067 --> 00:11:26.167
Okay.


00:11:27.100 --> 00:11:30.833
Uh... God is good. God is great.


00:11:32.067 --> 00:11:33.033
May He bless...


00:11:33.368 --> 00:11:38.100
May He bless
this house and the... this food.


00:11:38.134 --> 00:11:39.634
- Amen.
- Amen.


00:11:39.667 --> 00:11:40.667
- Amen.
- Amen.


00:11:42.966 --> 00:11:44.432
Erin, pass me your dish.


00:11:47.799 --> 00:11:49.466
Honey, will you
go get the water?


00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:51.100
I forgot the... the water.


00:11:51.399 --> 00:11:52.834
- You all right?
- Yeah.


00:11:52.866 --> 00:11:54.466
I just forgot the water pitcher.


00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:56.432
How's your mom doing, Erin?


00:11:56.466 --> 00:11:58.134
She's doing good.


00:11:58.167 --> 00:12:00.466
That's good. Is that enough?


00:12:05.667 --> 00:12:10.000
- Oh, it's terrible. Okay, I...
- ...I knew it.


00:12:10.033 --> 00:12:11.167
Well...


00:12:11.201 --> 00:12:13.000
