If you can convince
two psychiatrists


00:20:32.901 --> 00:20:34.000
that you're suicidal,


00:20:34.467 --> 00:20:36.599
the hospital
will have no choice.


00:20:36.634 --> 00:20:37.967
You'll get your abortion.


00:20:38.467 --> 00:20:42.599
Joy... do you think
you might be suicidal?


00:20:43.400 --> 00:20:46.967
Yes, Doctor.


00:20:48.467 --> 00:20:49.532
I might be.


00:20:49.834 --> 00:20:53.432
You know,
shotguns are very long.


00:20:53.467 --> 00:20:55.733
You'd have to place
the barrel under your jaw


00:20:56.101 --> 00:20:58.067
and pull the trigger
with your toe.


00:20:58.101 --> 00:21:00.599
You know, like...
Like Hemingway did.


00:21:01.101 --> 00:21:05.834
Yes. Yes, that's...
That's my plan. Mm-hmm.


00:21:15.967 --> 00:21:18.767
If the other psychiatrist
doesn't agree,


00:21:19.967 --> 00:21:21.500
this is your Plan B.


00:21:26.799 --> 00:21:29.101
See you then.


00:21:29.134 --> 00:21:31.733
Hi. Come here.


00:21:35.467 --> 00:21:37.166
Just fall down a staircase.


00:21:37.567 --> 00:21:40.901
It worked for me.


00:21:40.933 --> 00:21:43.599
Dr. Campbell's office? Mm-hmm.


00:22:36.567 --> 00:22:41.067
Oh! Oh! Oh!


00:22:44.634 --> 00:22:45.901
Mom?


00:22:45.933 --> 00:22:47.767
I'm fine. I'm fine.
I'm fine. I'm fine.


00:22:47.799 --> 00:22:49.901
- What did you do? What did you...
- I'm fine. I'm fine.


00:22:49.933 --> 00:22:51.634
I just slipped.


00:22:52.967 --> 00:22:55.767
I just slipped.
I just slipped.


00:22:58.500 --> 00:23:00.166
I just slipped. I just slipped.


00:23:00.733 --> 00:23:03.532
- Are you sure?
- I'm fine.


00:23:04.967 --> 00:23:06.834
I'm fine. I'm fine.


00:24:02.666 --> 00:24:04.967
He sees you.


00:24:05.432 --> 00:24:06.866
Best not to keep him waiting.


00:24:07.634 --> 00:24:08.599
Oh.


00:24:11.799 --> 00:24:12.634
Good morning.


00:24:12.967 --> 00:24:17.134
I would like to cash this check
for my husband, please.


00:24:29.134 --> 00:24:31.599
Of course, Mrs. Griffin.
One moment, please.


00:25:03.166 --> 00:25:05.400
Would you like to
recount yourself, Mrs. Griffin?


00:25:07.067 --> 00:25:11.034
No. I'm sure it's fine.
Thank you.


00:25:29.799 --> 00:25:32.201
Hey!
Playing those games, huh?


00:25:36.500 --> 00:25:38.166
It's gettin' time to
get you outta that skirt,


00:25:38.201 --> 00:25:39.000
little lady.


00:25:41.700 --> 00:25:43.834
Can't let
those legs go to waste, huh?


00:26:16.233 --> 00:26:19.599
I'm here for the,
uh, for the service?


00:27:19.634 --> 00:27:22.967
Uh, I'm... I'm sorry... I'm sorry.


00:27:31.432 --> 00:27:34.866
Looking good!


00:27:34.901 --> 00:27:36.567
Where are you going?


00:28:32.233 --> 00:28:34.901
How can you do that?


00:28:37.166 --> 00:28:38.733
How can you just keep going?


00:28:44.034 --> 00:28:45.067
It's what I do.


00:28:47.866 --> 00:28:49.166
It's what I've always done.


00:28:52.500 --> 00:28:55.567
It's what I will always do.


00:28:59.166 --> 00:29:01.101
I don't know how to fix this.


00:29:03.233 --> 00:29:04.467
I do.


00:29:16.799 --> 00:29:18.034
<i>Hello, this is Jane.</i>


00:29:19.700 --> 00:29:20.634
Jane who?


00:29:21.467 --> 00:29:24.767
<i>We're a service
for women who are expecting.</i>


00:29:43.634 --> 00:29:47.532
<i>- Hello, this is Jane.</i>
- I'm sorry.


00:29:47.567 --> 00:29:49.567
<i>Everyone hangs up
the first time.</i>


00:29:52.134 --> 00:29:53.901
So, how... how does it work?


00:30:10.767 --> 00:30:12.101
- Joy?
- Yes.


00:30:12.134 --> 00:30:13.432
Get in.


00:30:14.334 --> 00:30:17.034
No, this is not a taxi.
You sit up front with me.


00:30:18.067 --> 00:30:19.134
Oh.


00:30:25.067 --> 00:30:26.034
Right.


00:30:35.467 --> 00:30:38.532
So, uh, you must be Jane?


00:30:39.000 --> 00:30:40.134
I'm Gwen.


00:30:41.567 --> 00:30:42.599
Oh.


00:30:44.834 --> 00:30:45.834
When do I meet Jane?


00:30:46.834 --> 00:30:47.967
It's hard to say.


00:30:49.666 --> 00:30:51.134
How did you find us?


00:30:53.467 --> 00:30:55.733
Bus stop. Wicker Park.


00:30:56.432 --> 00:30:59.400
Wicker Park? No kidding.
You got family there?


00:31:03.500 --> 00:31:07.166
All right.


00:31:07.866 --> 00:31:12.500
Put this on. Cover your eyes.
Can't take any chances.


00:31:33.067 --> 00:31:34.101
I got you.


00:31:36.166 --> 00:31:38.901
Hold onto my arm.
It's a short walk.


00:31:54.101 --> 00:31:57.034
Hey. Careful.


00:32:04.866 --> 00:32:06.666
You can take
the blindfold off now.


00:32:09.767 --> 00:32:11.166
Thank you.


00:32:11.201 --> 00:32:13.733
Don't worry about it,
and I'll take the cash now.


00:32:17.700 --> 00:32:19.432
- Thank you.
- Six... Six hundred.


00:32:20.101 --> 00:32:22.967
- It's... It's all there.
- I know.


00:32:27.166 --> 00:32:30.101
Okay.


00:33:03.101 --> 00:33:05.933
I thought about bailing too.


00:33:10.166 --> 00:33:11.532
But I didn't.


00:33:12.967 --> 00:33:15.067
And he's the best that we have.


00:33:15.101 --> 00:33:18.000
A capitalist pig, but still...


00:33:21.166 --> 00:33:22.532
You cool with this?


00:33:25.834 --> 00:33:28.666
- Yes. Yes.
- Good. Okay.


00:33:28.700 --> 00:33:30.034
I'll be right outside that door.


00:33:30.067 --> 00:33:31.166
No, you... you...


00:33:31.201 --> 00:33:33.567
- You're not gonna stay?
- That's between you and the doc.


00:33:37.166 --> 00:33:38.467
Okay.


00:33:40.866 --> 00:33:42.166
She's ready.


00:33:42.201 --> 00:33:43.767
Just a minute, please.


00:34:56.800 --> 00:34:58.567
- What are you doing?
- Oh. It...


00:34:59.268 --> 00:35:01.800
- It just... It wasn't tucked.
- Thank you.


00:35:01.833 --> 00:35:04.400
But, you know,
someone comes in and does that.


00:35:06.001 --> 00:35:07.500
Are you a cop?


00:35:09.699 --> 00:35:11.532
- What?
- Please answer the question.


00:35:13.800 --> 00:35:14.699
No.


00:35:16.699 --> 00:35:19.067
I'm not...
I'm not a cop. No.


00:35:19.567 --> 00:35:23.467
Okay. Great.


00:35:24.034 --> 00:35:25.699
So, remove your skirt,
your underwear,


00:35:25.733 --> 00:35:26.967
put on this smock,


00:35:27.001 --> 00:35:29.134
and, uh, lie on the table,
please. Thank you.


00:36:04.833 --> 00:36:06.432
Please.


00:36:12.634 --> 00:36:14.733
- All right, scooch forward.
- Oh.


00:36:15.101 --> 00:36:16.500
There we go.


00:36:18.766 --> 00:36:21.500
- Oh. So cold.
- Yeah.


00:36:21.532 --> 00:36:22.967
Police have to tell you
they're police


00:36:23.001 --> 00:36:24.900
if you ask them directly.
Lean back.


00:36:39.849 --> 00:36:40.884
Password?


00:36:42.717 --> 00:36:44.750
Sanger.


00:36:48.983 --> 00:36:50.849
The password is overkill.


00:36:50.884 --> 00:36:53.817
Overkill is keeping
our asses out of jail.


00:36:53.849 --> 00:36:56.351
- Uh, it's Joy, right?
- Yes.


00:36:56.384 --> 00:36:58.849
Just have a seat right here.


00:36:59.451 --> 00:37:01.184
Virginia's making spaghetti.


00:37:01.217 --> 00:37:02.916
And there was
going to be a salad,


00:37:02.949 --> 00:37:05.983
but my spinach went slimy.


00:37:06.016 --> 00:37:08.016
Some women
get the chills afterward,


00:37:08.050 --> 00:37:09.217
but it passes quickly.


00:37:10.284 --> 00:37:12.150
Okay, this is for your cramps.


00:37:12.184 --> 00:37:15.217
- Oh. They're not that bad.
- It gets worse.


00:37:18.317 --> 00:37:21.384
So, um,
which one of you is Jane?


00:37:21.416 --> 00:37:23.849
Nobody's Jane.


00:37:23.884 --> 00:37:25.184
We're all Jane.


00:37:26.016 --> 00:37:27.451
Virginia started it.


00:37:27.483 --> 00:37:28.916
Help yourself.


00:37:28.949 --> 00:37:30.384
Uh, I didn't mean to.


00:37:30.416 --> 00:37:34.150
A friend called.
I found her a safe doctor.


00:37:34.184 --> 00:37:35.916
And then her friend called,


00:37:35.949 --> 00:37:40.251
and then her friend's friend,
and, uh, here we are.


00:37:40.983 --> 00:37:42.916
This will get
your blood sugar up,


00:37:42.949 --> 00:37:45.016
and then you're gonna rest
for a few hours.


00:37:45.050 --> 00:37:50.983
Oh... I'm... I'm...
I'm really... fine.


00:37:52.483 --> 00:37:53.717
You're one of those.


00:37:54.351 --> 00:37:55.050
One of what?


00:37:55.583 --> 00:37:58.750
Uh, I'll-be-home-in-an-hour-
and-I-don't-need-help type.


00:37:59.217 --> 00:38:02.682
Um, you could've
used some salt or something.


00:38:02.717 --> 00:38:06.184
- You know, it has basil in it.
- There's not enough.


00:38:06.217 --> 00:38:10.949
"Hoaxy" is not a word,
you cheating sack of shit.


00:38:10.983 --> 00:38:12.682
Where's our dictionary?


00:38:12.717 --> 00:38:14.750
You're kidding me, doll.


00:38:14.782 --> 00:38:17.682
How do we not have a dictionary?


00:38:17.717 --> 00:38:20.251
Because by the time
I finished haggling with the mob


00:38:20.284 --> 00:38:23.916
to get a decent rent on
this place and the other place,


00:38:23.949 --> 00:38:28.351
and paying for it with money
scrounged from rich ladies,


00:38:28.384 --> 00:38:32.083
no offense, Joy,
a dictionary was not a priority.


00:38:32.117 --> 00:38:34.184
- Well, excuse me.
- Okay, let's ask Joy.


00:38:34.217 --> 00:38:36.083
- Okay.
- Joy. "Hoaxy."


00:38:36.117 --> 00:38:38.284
Resembling or pertaining
to a hoax.


00:38:38.317 --> 00:38:40.717
That sure is hoaxy.


00:38:40.750 --> 00:38:42.717
Come on.


00:38:45.916 --> 00:38:48.849
- No. Come on.
- Right. See? No.


00:38:49.884 --> 00:38:51.717
All right.


00:38:51.750 --> 00:38:53.884
Pregnancy fills you
with hormones.


00:38:53.916 --> 00:38:55.050
Over the next few days,


00:38:55.083 --> 00:38:56.384
they're going to
leave your body.


00:38:56.416 --> 00:38:58.184
You're going to feel
really, really sad.


00:38:58.217 --> 00:39:00.416
It's okay. It's normal.


00:39:02.217 --> 00:39:03.150
Thank you.


00:39:04.150 --> 00:39:06.884
- For everything.
- Eat.


00:39:06.916 --> 00:39:10.083
Eat and then sleep
and then scram.


00:39:14.849 --> 00:39:16.351
Okay, trust me.


00:39:16.782 --> 00:39:18.184
I don't trust you.


00:39:22.050 --> 00:39:24.916
Last night I started cramping,


00:39:24.949 --> 00:39:28.983
and, uh, I took some
of the pills Dr. Falk gave me.


00:39:31.050 --> 00:39:34.949
Um, the cramps were gone
this morning.


00:39:36.717 --> 00:39:40.083
But then after lunch,
I went to the bathroom...


00:39:43.117 --> 00:39:46.849
and there was... blood.


00:39:47.317 --> 00:39:48.717
There was a lot of blood.


00:39:51.083 --> 00:39:52.416
It happened very fast.


00:39:54.483 --> 00:39:56.117
I lost the baby, Charlotte.


00:39:57.117 --> 00:39:58.050
She's in heaven.


00:40:01.117 --> 00:40:01.916
Don't say that.


00:40:02.217 --> 00:40:04.050
Sweetheart, it's only natural
to feel this way...


00:40:04.083 --> 00:40:05.817
Stop that!
Stop telling me how to feel.


00:40:07.983 --> 00:40:09.251
Leave her be.


00:40:13.217 --> 00:40:14.317
Miscarriage?


00:40:19.251 --> 00:40:20.916
I'd like to talk to the doctor.


00:40:23.184 --> 00:40:25.416
I'm so sorry, Will.


00:40:27.483 --> 00:40:28.849
It's not your fault.


00:40:32.884 --> 00:40:34.251
It's nobody's fault.


00:40:39.451 --> 00:40:41.150
Have some of that, all right.


00:40:43.016 --> 00:40:46.717
Help with the... pain.


00:40:49.317 --> 00:40:51.050
<i>A man who has spent years...</i>


00:40:51.083 --> 00:40:52.884
I got it.


00:40:54.817 --> 00:40:55.849
Hello?


00:40:57.351 --> 00:40:59.083
Yeah, hold on one sec.


00:40:59.117 --> 00:41:00.916
It's Fran from the PTA.


00:41:03.916 --> 00:41:05.949
- Hello?
<i>- How's the bleeding?</i>


00:41:05.983 --> 00:41:07.949
Remember,
if it's stopped already,


00:41:07.983 --> 00:41:08.949
it will start again.


00:41:08.983 --> 00:41:09.916
Soon.


00:41:12.184 --> 00:41:13.949
Well, say something.
It's Virginia.


00:41:13.983 --> 00:41:15.717
<i>Uh, yes. Uh, I know.</i>


00:41:16.117 --> 00:41:18.682
We do our first checkup call
on day three.


00:41:19.317 --> 00:41:20.916
<i>What, is he
standing right there?</i>


00:41:20.949 --> 00:41:22.884
Uh, well, I agree
that the playground


00:41:22.916 --> 00:41:23.750
needs to be remodeled.


00:41:24.184 --> 00:41:26.782
I just don't think a bake sale
is gonna raise enough funds.


00:41:26.817 --> 00:41:28.983
<i>Ooh, you are good at that, Joy.</i>


00:41:29.016 --> 00:41:30.251
<i>You got potential.</i>


00:41:30.284 --> 00:41:31.949
<i>So, are you taking
your antibiotics?</i>


00:41:31.983 --> 00:41:34.384
- Of course.
<i>- Any chills? Fever?</i>


00:41:34.416 --> 00:41:35.817
No, he's gone.


00:41:36.617 --> 00:41:40.217
I want to be sure you're healing
on schedule and coping.


00:41:41.050 --> 00:41:44.217
Uh, I... I think I am.


00:41:45.184 --> 00:41:46.050
How will I know?


00:41:46.317 --> 00:41:49.317
Well, you can't, but you'll know
when you're better.


00:41:49.351 --> 00:41:51.717
So, listen,
I know it's short notice,


00:41:51.750 --> 00:41:53.983
but, um,
since you're feeling okay,


00:41:54.016 --> 00:41:56.016
I got a bit
of an emergency down here.


00:41:56.050 --> 00:41:58.284
Our morning driver came down
with food poisoning,


00:41:58.317 --> 00:41:59.682
and it's a mess.


00:41:59.717 --> 00:42:02.251
I got a girl waiting
not far from you.


00:42:02.284 --> 00:42:04.150
<i>Can you pick her up
and run her in?</i>


00:42:04.184 --> 00:42:08.251
No, that...
That's not a good idea.


00:42:08.284 --> 00:42:10.983
<i>You do have a car,
right? Hubby takes the L?</i>


00:42:12.184 --> 00:42:14.050
Well, he... he does, but...


00:42:14.083 --> 00:42:16.916
Onetime deal. Drop her off.
Never hear from us again.


00:42:17.251 --> 00:42:19.150
Virginia, I am...


00:42:19.184 --> 00:42:21.284
Thanks. You are a lifesaver.


00:42:21.317 --> 00:42:23.016
Gwen's gonna call
with instructions.


00:42:23.050 --> 00:42:24.083
<i>No. I...</i>


00:42:25.949 --> 00:42:27.682
All right.


00:42:27.717 --> 00:42:29.016
Did you take a bite out of this?


00:42:29.050 --> 00:42:29.949
No.


00:42:31.916 --> 00:42:33.817
I hope the doctor is handsome.


00:42:36.117 --> 00:42:37.682
Does it matter?


00:42:37.717 --> 00:42:40.849
It's kind of
embarrassing, the whole thing.


00:42:40.884 --> 00:42:43.916
So it might as well be
something to look at.


00:42:47.050 --> 00:42:50.083
Wouldn't it be funny if I fell
in love with my abortion doctor?


00:42:54.782 --> 00:42:56.351
I'm supposed to collect the fee.


00:42:57.117 --> 00:42:59.384
Oh, right.


00:43:01.251 --> 00:43:03.117
Only date men with money.


00:43:05.150 --> 00:43:08.750
He was my boss
at the bank. He's married.


00:43:09.583 --> 00:43:12.150
I asked him to pull out,
but I don't think they can


00:43:12.184 --> 00:43:14.650
at a certain point, can they?


00:43:16.416 --> 00:43:18.451
He said, "I'll take care of it."


00:43:18.483 --> 00:43:19.849
And he did.


00:43:21.949 --> 00:43:23.184
Have you ever done this?


00:43:25.949 --> 00:43:27.016
No.


00:43:30.050 --> 00:43:32.916
You're very tightly wound, Joy.


00:43:37.416 --> 00:43:40.717
- It's a lot of money.
- Not as much as having a baby.


00:43:42.384 --> 00:43:45.083
Virginia ran out
of our activist dykes?


00:43:46.416 --> 00:43:48.083
I'm doing her a favor.


00:43:49.416 --> 00:43:50.717
We've met, actually.


00:43:51.451 --> 00:43:52.650
I'm Joy.


00:43:53.983 --> 00:43:56.750
Right. Sure. Yeah.


00:43:56.782 --> 00:43:59.782
I had a slightly different view
last time. Excuse me.


00:44:04.150 --> 00:44:06.184
I'll just have you lie down
for a while.


00:44:06.682 --> 00:44:08.717
Well done, Jackie O.


00:44:09.682 --> 00:44:12.384
I'm sorry if that wasn't
the morning you expected.


00:44:15.050 --> 00:44:17.416
You read my mind, doll.


00:44:17.983 --> 00:44:21.150
Mmm-mmm-mmm. I'm trying to quit.


00:44:22.717 --> 00:44:23.650
Why?


00:44:24.284 --> 00:44:27.083
Maybe I wanna sing opera
for my next life.


00:44:29.050 --> 00:44:32.317
We have organizing meetings
on Thursdays.


00:44:34.150 --> 00:44:35.983
That's the address.


00:44:42.483 --> 00:44:44.384
I don't agree with
what you're doing.


00:44:45.217 --> 00:44:46.284
That girl...


00:44:47.317 --> 00:44:48.384
What about her?


00:44:48.416 --> 00:44:52.351
She's having sex
without protection.


00:44:52.384 --> 00:44:54.916
She's sleeping with
a married man


00:44:55.284 --> 00:44:56.916
who paid for the procedure.


00:44:58.083 --> 00:45:01.983
- She's so...
- ...unconcerned.


00:45:02.016 --> 00:45:05.351
We help women.
We don't ask questions.


00:45:06.083 --> 00:45:09.317
And if we judged everyone
by how they present themselves,


00:45:09.849 --> 00:45:12.916
I might write you off
as a lightweight housewife


00:45:12.949 --> 00:45:15.117
who bakes
mediocre snickerdoodles


00:45:15.150 --> 00:45:18.083
and gets plastered
on four o'clock martinis.


00:45:20.384 --> 00:45:23.849
It's chocolate chip, usually.


00:45:25.384 --> 00:45:28.983
Thanks for helping out.
I really do appreciate it.


00:45:32.817 --> 00:45:36.351
I make the best coffee.


00:46:22.016 --> 00:46:25.317
Well, well, well.
Look what the Sister dragged in.


00:46:25.351 --> 00:46:28.117
Cookies! Thank Christ!


00:46:28.384 --> 00:46:29.949
Are those snickerdoodles?


00:46:29.983 --> 00:46:32.949
Uh, they're not my specialty,
but I had a request.


00:46:33.916 --> 00:46:37.849
We were just about
to start the cards. Have a seat.


00:46:39.384 --> 00:46:44.016
- How you doing? Okay?
- Mm. Yes. I... Yeah.


00:46:44.050 --> 00:46:45.884
My husband offered me ice.


00:46:45.916 --> 00:46:49.217
- Oh, God. Ice.
- Take it away, Maeve.


00:46:49.550 --> 00:46:53.184
Uh, Joanne, 29.
LMP eight weeks ago.


