01:08:27.618 --> 01:08:32.016
I just felt like
you deserve a non-frozen meal.


01:08:32.050 --> 01:08:33.917
- Wow, babe, wow.
- Mm-hmm.


01:08:33.949 --> 01:08:36.083
And you know
I'm lousy at Italian, so...


01:08:36.117 --> 01:08:37.884
You're not lousy
at Italian, but...


01:08:37.917 --> 01:08:39.117
Yeah, but I don't
do those meatballs


01:08:39.150 --> 01:08:40.283
like they do the meatballs.


01:08:41.150 --> 01:08:42.417
Come here.


01:08:42.451 --> 01:08:45.949
- Honey, the door.
- It's fine.


01:08:47.117 --> 01:08:48.251
It's locked.


01:08:49.984 --> 01:08:51.117
How's art class goin'?


01:08:52.884 --> 01:08:55.917
Oh, ah, goodness.
So much work.


01:08:56.984 --> 01:08:58.417
Ah, but it's wonderful.


01:08:58.783 --> 01:09:00.850
How come
you never bring anything home?


01:09:03.083 --> 01:09:04.417
Oh, honey, I...


01:09:05.984 --> 01:09:08.783
Nothing I paint is worth
bringing home. Believe me.


01:09:09.649 --> 01:09:13.251
Well, maybe I'd like one of
your paintings for my room.


01:09:13.884 --> 01:09:16.083
I mean, it's okay
if you don't want to.


01:09:21.484 --> 01:09:24.016
Thank you
for making me feel like Picasso.


01:09:26.484 --> 01:09:29.016
Don't push it, Mom.


01:10:56.451 --> 01:10:58.850
I want to learn
the entire procedure.


01:11:01.750 --> 01:11:04.216
You're gonna teach me.


01:11:06.216 --> 01:11:07.917
Sure. Yeah, why not?


01:11:09.884 --> 01:11:11.417
Maybe after that,
you can ask someone else


01:11:11.451 --> 01:11:14.050
to teach you open-heart surgery,
brain surgery, you know?


01:11:17.083 --> 01:11:18.283
Sure, why not?


01:11:19.016 --> 01:11:21.716
Do you think just anybody
can pick it up on a whim?


01:11:22.949 --> 01:11:24.817
Well, you obviously did.


01:11:28.184 --> 01:11:29.949
Because you're not a doctor.


01:11:33.984 --> 01:11:35.384
You want me
to show you my medical degree?


01:11:36.917 --> 01:11:39.251
- Well, that would be a trick.
- Excuse me?


01:11:39.817 --> 01:11:42.984
The university has no record


01:11:43.016 --> 01:11:45.083
of you ever attending
medical school there,


01:11:45.783 --> 01:11:48.083
which makes sense
when you think about it.


01:11:48.618 --> 01:11:50.682
Why would a real doctor


01:11:51.451 --> 01:11:53.817
risk his medical license


01:11:54.551 --> 01:11:57.417
performing illegal abortions
out of a run-down apartment?


01:11:57.451 --> 01:11:58.716
Hey!


01:11:59.917 --> 01:12:01.317
I keep a very pristine shop.


01:12:02.716 --> 01:12:03.850
Thank you very much.


01:12:05.884 --> 01:12:07.716
Maybe I care about
the women, huh?


01:12:09.783 --> 01:12:10.984
You ever think about that?


01:12:11.682 --> 01:12:15.682
If that were true,
you would charge a lot less.


01:12:15.716 --> 01:12:17.384
My fee is entirely reasonable.


01:12:17.417 --> 01:12:19.216
You have a swimming pool.


01:12:20.850 --> 01:12:22.184
I'm the best you've got.


01:12:28.317 --> 01:12:31.283
Don't make me tell Virginia
you're not a real doctor.


01:12:33.484 --> 01:12:34.850
You're going to teach me...


01:12:36.949 --> 01:12:38.016
please.


01:12:40.317 --> 01:12:41.649
Please.


01:13:02.016 --> 01:13:04.317
Lesson one.


01:13:06.484 --> 01:13:08.184
You ever scoop seeds
out of a pumpkin?


01:13:09.083 --> 01:13:10.850
Uh, sure.


01:13:12.283 --> 01:13:13.417
It's like that.


01:13:14.716 --> 01:13:16.716
For most of the procedures
that I do.


01:13:19.050 --> 01:13:21.117
...age 35 in Chicago...


01:13:54.750 --> 01:13:56.050
Are we havin' a party?


01:13:57.783 --> 01:14:02.016
A bake sale. Uh... you know.


01:14:02.050 --> 01:14:03.884
Did you make extra for us?


01:14:03.917 --> 01:14:06.317
Sure. Yes. Let's...
I'll get you a plate.


01:14:06.350 --> 01:14:08.783
Okay, terrific.
They look delicious.


01:14:10.417 --> 01:14:11.984
Okay, one more shot.


01:14:12.451 --> 01:14:15.384
This is to keep you
from bleeding too much.


01:14:15.417 --> 01:14:17.817
It's a nice, easy one.


01:14:21.716 --> 01:14:22.917
- Ready?
- Hmm.


01:14:22.949 --> 01:14:24.682
Okay, let's take a deep breath.


01:14:25.251 --> 01:14:29.716
Breathe in... and out.


01:14:33.083 --> 01:14:34.117
That's it.


01:14:37.050 --> 01:14:38.850
It takes a minute to kick in.


01:14:44.083 --> 01:14:45.184
Come here.


01:15:14.216 --> 01:15:15.850
- Like that?
- Mm-hmm.


01:15:19.783 --> 01:15:21.317
Don't make me regret this.


01:15:34.716 --> 01:15:36.884
It's not that hard, Virginia.


01:15:37.583 --> 01:15:40.949
I could do it myself.
You could do it.


01:15:40.984 --> 01:15:43.451
What are you smoking?
We're not doctors, Joy.


01:15:43.484 --> 01:15:46.716
- Neither is Dean.
- What?


01:15:47.716 --> 01:15:51.384
Oh, shit. Oh, I promised
I wasn't gonna tell you that.


01:15:52.050 --> 01:15:54.283
- Holy shit.
- It's not rocket science.


01:15:54.716 --> 01:15:56.451
It's a 20-minute procedure


01:15:56.484 --> 01:15:58.083
that a man with
no medical training


01:15:58.117 --> 01:15:58.884
taught himself.


01:15:59.350 --> 01:16:02.016
- Safer than a tonsillectomy.
- Which is done by a surgeon.


01:16:02.317 --> 01:16:04.216
We could do this.


01:16:04.251 --> 01:16:07.251
We could do
the procedures for free.


01:16:07.283 --> 01:16:10.384
No. No way. It's too risky.


01:16:10.417 --> 01:16:12.716
We take on risk
every time we answer that phone.


01:16:12.750 --> 01:16:15.117
No, we minimize risk.
We're careful.


01:16:15.150 --> 01:16:15.984
We pay off the right monster.


01:16:16.317 --> 01:16:18.949
So you think it's an accident
we haven't been busted?


01:16:23.949 --> 01:16:25.083
You're right.


01:16:27.083 --> 01:16:31.750
But we are entirely dependent
on one man who is not a doctor.


01:16:32.083 --> 01:16:35.283
If I were to let you do this
and you screwed up one time,


01:16:35.949 --> 01:16:38.817
if even one woman
died on our watch,


01:16:39.484 --> 01:16:41.216
I mean, think about that.


01:16:42.384 --> 01:16:45.716
Not to mention,
it's felony homicide.


01:16:46.817 --> 01:16:47.783
Okay?


01:16:51.016 --> 01:16:53.884
I'm not scared of jail, Joy.
I've been to jail.


01:16:54.484 --> 01:16:57.750
I'm scared there won't be
anyone left to answer the phone.


01:17:01.283 --> 01:17:03.083
It's supposed to be
a shepherd's pie,


01:17:03.117 --> 01:17:04.750
but it's more like
hamburger noodles.


01:17:05.884 --> 01:17:07.317
Mmm, it's delicious, Char.


01:17:09.150 --> 01:17:12.716
- Don't you think so, Joy?
- Mm-hmm. Perfection.


01:17:16.716 --> 01:17:18.184
I tell you what, I wish...


01:17:18.216 --> 01:17:20.417
I wish I learned to make
hamburger noodles in school.


01:17:21.016 --> 01:17:22.984
I don't think
you mean that, Will.


01:17:24.716 --> 01:17:26.317
You're saying it to be nice,
and it is nice.


01:17:26.350 --> 01:17:28.117
And it's also true
that it tastes good.


01:17:28.150 --> 01:17:29.050
But...


01:17:29.716 --> 01:17:32.083
we're pretty sure you don't wish
you'd learned it in school.


01:17:32.117 --> 01:17:32.917
Because as a man,


01:17:33.150 --> 01:17:34.317
Home Ec would have been
a waste of your time.


01:17:34.350 --> 01:17:39.117
You had, um, wrestling shop
and grooming for law school,


01:17:39.150 --> 01:17:40.917
which is fantastic.


01:17:41.618 --> 01:17:43.451
But our daughter's spending
her school hours


01:17:43.484 --> 01:17:45.716
learning what order
to do the dishes in.


01:17:48.283 --> 01:17:49.817
Did something happen today?


01:17:51.117 --> 01:17:53.150
Something upsetting?


01:17:53.551 --> 01:17:56.884
No. I had a great day.


01:17:57.350 --> 01:17:59.251
I like Home Ec.


01:17:59.649 --> 01:18:02.317
So did I,
but that's not my point.


01:18:07.484 --> 01:18:09.283
Uh, in case there's any doubt,


01:18:10.016 --> 01:18:11.949
I'd like to
go on record and say...


01:18:13.083 --> 01:18:14.949
women can be
whatever they want to be.


01:18:15.583 --> 01:18:17.984
As long as you don't have
to eat too many TV dinners.


01:18:18.016 --> 01:18:21.283
- Okay, that's not fair. Come on.
- I totally agree.


01:18:22.050 --> 01:18:24.984
I'm gonna heat up
the pumpkin pie. All right?


01:18:25.016 --> 01:18:26.384
Just get it in the oven.


01:18:31.949 --> 01:18:33.117
What are you laughing at?


01:18:34.451 --> 01:18:35.216
Oh.


01:18:35.251 --> 01:18:37.216
These are the people
who can pay.


01:18:37.251 --> 01:18:41.184
And these are the people
who cannot pay.


01:18:41.216 --> 01:18:43.750
We need an answering machine.


01:18:43.783 --> 01:18:45.716
Or I don't know what.


01:18:45.750 --> 01:18:48.283
I mean, there are only
two free a week.


01:18:48.317 --> 01:18:50.451
How are we going
to get through them all in time?


01:18:50.484 --> 01:18:52.850
How are we gonna decide
who gets the freebies?


01:18:53.817 --> 01:18:56.184
Oh, this one. We have to do her.


01:18:56.216 --> 01:18:57.050
She was raped.


01:18:57.384 --> 01:19:00.350
All of the free slots have gone
to rape victims lately.


01:19:00.384 --> 01:19:02.050
- So what?
- I mean, is that it?


01:19:02.083 --> 01:19:03.251
Is that the deciding factor?


01:19:03.283 --> 01:19:05.117
If you were raped,
you get a free slot?


01:19:05.150 --> 01:19:07.050
Are you saying
they don't deserve the slots?


01:19:07.083 --> 01:19:08.716
Of course not.


01:19:08.750 --> 01:19:10.949
I'm saying that this
11-year-old girl deserves it.


01:19:10.984 --> 01:19:11.783
Oh, my God.


01:19:12.150 --> 01:19:14.716
And this mother of eight
who's being evicted deserves it.


01:19:14.750 --> 01:19:15.884
She was raped.


01:19:15.917 --> 01:19:17.083
Okay, I can't have this fight.


01:19:17.117 --> 01:19:19.850
Well, this lady has cancer
and she can't continue her chemo


01:19:19.884 --> 01:19:20.649
while she's pregnant.


01:19:20.949 --> 01:19:24.783
- Yeah, that's noble.
- I vote for Rita.


01:19:24.817 --> 01:19:27.783
She's finishing her dissertation
on homelessness


01:19:27.817 --> 01:19:30.251
in American cities.
Think of the good she could do.


01:19:30.283 --> 01:19:32.317
- She was raped!
- Okay.


01:19:32.350 --> 01:19:36.917
This is just fucked up. I mean,
at least before we just got rid


01:19:36.949 --> 01:19:39.384
of everybody who couldn't pay.


01:19:39.417 --> 01:19:41.850
Look, it has to be random.


01:19:41.884 --> 01:19:43.783
We are not making
value judgments


01:19:43.817 --> 01:19:44.984
about these women.


01:19:45.016 --> 01:19:47.682
- That's not how we work.
- That's bullshit!


01:19:47.716 --> 01:19:49.283
It's life or death
for some of them.


01:19:49.317 --> 01:19:51.417
It's life or death
for all of them.


01:19:54.384 --> 01:19:55.783
You get one shot.


01:19:58.850 --> 01:20:00.317
Have you seen my keys?


01:20:00.350 --> 01:20:01.984
Why are you so jumpy?


01:20:03.083 --> 01:20:04.150
I'm not.


01:20:07.884 --> 01:20:09.016
It's Sunday. Relax.


01:20:09.283 --> 01:20:10.384
Did your father
happen to mention


01:20:10.417 --> 01:20:12.682
when he's coming back from golf?


01:20:12.716 --> 01:20:13.884
Okay, where are you going?


01:20:14.716 --> 01:20:17.150
Well, I told you, honey,
a few of us from art class


01:20:17.184 --> 01:20:20.016
are meeting up to,
um, do a life study.


01:20:24.317 --> 01:20:26.317
You said lunch before.


01:20:26.783 --> 01:20:28.117
Then why did you ask?


01:20:32.484 --> 01:20:34.216
All right,
I'll see you this afternoon.


01:20:34.251 --> 01:20:35.682
Spaghetti for dinner.


01:20:42.117 --> 01:20:44.783
Prepare a hot bath
in a shallow pan


01:20:44.817 --> 01:20:45.949
to sterilize the instruments.


01:20:48.850 --> 01:20:49.884
Where's Joy?


01:20:52.317 --> 01:20:53.350
Ay, ay, ay.


01:21:07.350 --> 01:21:10.317
It's 11:20. Do you...
Do you think she chickened out?


01:21:11.251 --> 01:21:14.216
I will beat her to death
with a rolling pin.


01:21:16.350 --> 01:21:18.917
Should I call Dean?


01:21:21.984 --> 01:21:23.750
We thought you got cold feet.


01:21:23.783 --> 01:21:25.216
Oh, ye of little faith.


01:21:25.884 --> 01:21:27.884
Hope you've had your coffee.


01:21:34.417 --> 01:21:35.783
Where's the doctor?


01:21:36.251 --> 01:21:38.984
You've got to be kidding me.


01:21:39.016 --> 01:21:40.817
It wasn't some
kind of statement.


01:21:40.850 --> 01:21:42.682
She was just the next card.


01:21:43.884 --> 01:21:44.884
Karma.


01:22:05.384 --> 01:22:06.682
Thank you.


01:22:10.884 --> 01:22:13.283
I remember you.


01:22:15.050 --> 01:22:16.384
I remember you too.


01:22:18.150 --> 01:22:21.884
For the bleeding.


01:22:29.750 --> 01:22:31.117
I want to be a mom someday.


01:22:34.117 --> 01:22:37.283
You will be. Just not today.


01:22:38.150 --> 01:22:40.317
All right.


01:22:48.050 --> 01:22:49.283
I'm gonna dilate you now,


01:22:49.317 --> 01:22:52.984
which means opening the cervix,
so I can perform the extraction.


01:22:55.283 --> 01:22:57.283
Are you really
doing this yourself?


01:22:57.317 --> 01:22:59.384
Yes, but you know what?


01:22:59.417 --> 01:23:01.783
This is the first time
I've done it alone.


01:23:01.817 --> 01:23:02.949
You understand that, right?


01:23:04.716 --> 01:23:07.216
Who was your
first-grade teacher, Sandra?


01:23:07.783 --> 01:23:13.384
I don't...
I can't remember. Um...


01:23:15.184 --> 01:23:20.682
Oh, I think she was...
Miss Milligan.


01:23:21.117 --> 01:23:22.750
What did she look like?


01:23:23.750 --> 01:23:28.083
Uh, she had gray, curly hair,


01:23:28.117 --> 01:23:32.384
like little tight curls that
looked like a helmet.


01:23:32.417 --> 01:23:35.251
And all of her sweaters
were green.


01:23:35.283 --> 01:23:36.917
No kidding.


01:23:37.216 --> 01:23:38.850
How are you doing?
Are you okay?


01:23:38.884 --> 01:23:41.283
- Yeah.
- Just relax.


01:23:42.984 --> 01:23:47.283
Breathe.


01:23:51.417 --> 01:23:54.783
I'm gonna use the curette now.
You'll feel some pressure.


01:23:59.783 --> 01:24:01.384
Uh, how do you know
where everything is?


01:24:03.216 --> 01:24:06.682
I can't see it, so I visualize
what I know is there,


01:24:07.317 --> 01:24:08.817
and then I feel for it.


01:24:11.750 --> 01:24:13.350
Here we go.


01:24:13.917 --> 01:24:16.251
Deep breaths.


01:24:22.484 --> 01:24:24.083
He notices me.


01:24:25.317 --> 01:24:29.016
He makes me feel so... fine.


01:24:30.716 --> 01:24:32.451
He says if I love him,
I'll sleep with him.


01:24:32.484 --> 01:24:33.783
And if I don't,


01:24:34.184 --> 01:24:35.750
it's the worst bummer.


01:24:37.317 --> 01:24:38.783
And I want him to love me,


01:24:38.817 --> 01:24:41.283
but he just gets what he wants
and he walks away.


01:24:42.417 --> 01:24:43.649
I'm so stupid.


01:24:44.251 --> 01:24:46.016
You are not stupid, sweetheart.


01:24:46.949 --> 01:24:49.917
But he sounds like a jackass.


01:24:49.949 --> 01:24:53.216
I'll go.


01:24:54.884 --> 01:24:58.783
It's okay.
It's okay. You're doing great.


01:25:29.016 --> 01:25:31.884
I was... There's a... I'm just
setting up the life model.


01:25:31.917 --> 01:25:32.949
I told her.


01:25:49.350 --> 01:25:51.783
You got there all...
All by yourself?


01:25:52.682 --> 01:25:54.817
I know how to use
public transportation.


01:25:54.850 --> 01:25:56.016
It's not hard.


01:25:59.484 --> 01:26:01.884
And you wrote down
the address in your planner.


01:26:09.050 --> 01:26:11.949
I thought that you
might be having an affair.


01:26:11.984 --> 01:26:14.850
What? Oh, God. No.


01:26:15.850 --> 01:26:17.682
No. Never, Char. Never.


01:26:19.451 --> 01:26:20.783
I wish you were.


01:26:24.050 --> 01:26:26.283
I will answer any questions.


01:26:29.783 --> 01:26:32.117
I don't have any questions.
I don't want to know.


01:26:32.884 --> 01:26:36.750
It's just... I don't want
to know about babies dying,


01:26:36.783 --> 01:26:39.384
or people getting shot,
or periods, or Vietnam.


01:26:48.016 --> 01:26:49.350
It's an answering machine,


01:26:49.384 --> 01:26:51.283
so we don't miss
a single message.


01:26:52.216 --> 01:26:53.649
This thing is cutting edge.


01:26:54.518 --> 01:26:56.682
I told Dean
we don't need him anymore.


01:26:57.750 --> 01:26:58.850
You what?


01:26:58.884 --> 01:26:59.817
Yeah. You know,


01:26:59.850 --> 01:27:02.117
I have devoted
a lot of my life to causes.


01:27:02.150 --> 01:27:04.251
You name the cause, I was there.


01:27:04.283 --> 01:27:05.783
Marches,


01:27:05.984 --> 01:27:08.317
protests, sit-ins, and mostly,


01:27:08.350 --> 01:27:12.117
it was a bunch of guys screaming
Marxist theory at each other


01:27:12.150 --> 01:27:14.417
on the steps of City Hall
drowning all the women out.


01:27:14.451 --> 01:27:15.884
We did not have a voice.


01:27:16.783 --> 01:27:19.716
Turns out, the rats are
bigger pigs than the pigs.


01:27:25.150 --> 01:27:29.083
Do you think you can handle
20 procedures this week?


01:27:34.350 --> 01:27:36.817
- Yes.
- Yes?


01:27:38.283 --> 01:27:39.317
Yes!


01:27:46.251 --> 01:27:47.384
Okay.


01:29:28.817 --> 01:29:30.949
So, tell me
how you ladies came to be...


01:29:33.850 --> 01:29:34.783
Jane.


01:29:34.817 --> 01:29:35.917
Joy.


01:29:35.949 --> 01:29:37.884
My wife's name
is Joy, Detective.


01:29:38.850 --> 01:29:40.184
Yeah, you told me that.


01:29:48.050 --> 01:29:51.251
But a person contains...


01:29:54.384 --> 01:29:55.750
multitudes.


01:30:03.016 --> 01:30:04.283
Isn't that right, Joy?


01:30:07.949 --> 01:30:09.150
Maybe.


01:30:12.817 --> 01:30:13.949
Like you.


01:30:16.050 --> 01:30:17.884
- Hmm?
- How?


01:30:20.384 --> 01:30:22.283
- Vice.
- Hmm.


01:30:23.884 --> 01:30:25.016
Radicals.


01:30:27.150 --> 01:30:29.251
- Addicts.
- Hmm.


01:30:31.783 --> 01:30:34.783
You see, I enjoy the variety.


01:30:38.083 --> 01:30:41.682
And these threads? Just a means
to gettin' the job done.


01:30:43.050 --> 01:30:44.251
A mask, right?


01:30:46.917 --> 01:30:47.984
You wear a mask,


01:30:49.050 --> 01:30:50.050
don't you, Joy?


01:30:53.150 --> 01:30:55.750
And we have a mutual friend.
Helen Burr.


01:30:59.050 --> 01:31:00.050
No, I... I...


01:31:01.716 --> 01:31:03.251
I don't know
anyone named Helen Burr.


01:31:03.283 --> 01:31:05.184
Well, my old pal Carl,


01:31:05.216 --> 01:31:07.682
he's married to Helen.
He gives me a call.


01:31:07.716 --> 01:31:08.682
He says that


01:31:09.417 --> 01:31:12.817
she contacted you ladies
for a you-know-what.


01:31:12.850 --> 01:31:14.216
And it didn't work out.


01:31:14.716 --> 01:31:15.917
Couldn't afford you.


01:31:16.484 --> 01:31:19.384
Now, Helen,
she's a... good lady.


01:31:19.917 --> 01:31:21.917
She didn't give up any names,


01:31:22.618 --> 01:31:26.817
so nothin' except
that it wasn't... your fault.


01:31:32.283 --> 01:31:33.251
You see, she...


01:31:35.117 --> 01:31:37.350
stuck somethin' up her privates,


01:31:39.917 --> 01:31:41.783
somethin' that
didn't belong there.


01:31:44.451 --> 01:31:46.083
So she ended up in the hospital.


01:31:47.884 --> 01:31:48.984
Almost died.


01:31:56.484 --> 01:31:59.083
I don't know
anything about that.


01:32:01.783 --> 01:32:04.150
Sure. I didn't think you did.


01:32:06.949 --> 01:32:10.117
But there's this doctor
over at the hospital, Falk?


01:32:10.716 --> 01:32:14.783
Yeah,
he's my wife's obstetrician.


01:32:14.817 --> 01:32:18.184
He also happens to be
my brother-in-law.


01:32:18.750 --> 01:32:22.050
So, if I hypothetically
ask him to say


01:32:22.083 --> 01:32:26.917
that one of his patients
is up to somethin' shady,


01:32:26.949 --> 01:32:28.150
somethin' that almost got


01:32:28.184 --> 01:32:30.117
another one
of his patients killed...


01:32:30.150 --> 01:32:32.384
Look, officer, my wife has not...


01:32:32.417 --> 01:32:35.184
Has gotten so much
as a traffic ticket.


01:32:35.216 --> 01:32:37.884
I assure you,
she would never involve herself


01:32:37.917 --> 01:32:39.350
in something like this.


01:32:47.716 --> 01:32:49.050
Well, that's too bad.


01:33:14.083 --> 01:33:15.150
This woman...


01:33:17.384 --> 01:33:19.216
is going to call Jane,


01:33:19.984 --> 01:33:22.283
and Jane will provide her
with a service.


01:33:26.817 --> 01:33:28.117
She's a friend of mine.


01:33:29.783 --> 01:33:31.884
Lots of cops have friends,
you understand?


01:33:31.917 --> 01:33:33.884
Look, Detective, my wife,


01:33:33.917 --> 01:33:36.016
she doesn't know anything
about this, okay?


01:33:40.949 --> 01:33:42.117
There's a fee.


01:33:44.184 --> 01:33:47.649
- Five hundred, right?
- Six hundred.


01:33:55.050 --> 01:33:56.682
Just make sure that...


01:33:57.451 --> 01:34:00.184
Jane gets this message.


01:34:02.984 --> 01:34:04.649
Thank you, Mrs. Griffin.


01:34:06.083 --> 01:34:09.384
Oh, no. No.
I can see myself out.


01:34:28.117 --> 01:34:30.117
Is there any point
in me asking questions,


01:34:30.150 --> 01:34:31.750
or you're just gonna lie?


01:34:31.783 --> 01:34:33.783
Ask me whatever you need to ask.


01:35:01.083 --> 01:35:02.216
You...


01:35:05.050 --> 01:35:08.184
arrange illegal abortions?


01:35:09.817 --> 01:35:12.117
- Safe abortions.
- Oh, I don't even know...


01:35:15.283 --> 01:35:16.783
I don't even know.


01:35:18.817 --> 01:35:20.283
Do you want to end up in prison?


01:35:20.317 --> 01:35:23.083
- No, of course not.
- Joy, this is...


01:35:23.117 --> 01:35:26.451
You're an accessory
to multiple crimes.


01:35:26.484 --> 01:35:31.783
Maybe I think
we could get you immunity


01:35:31.817 --> 01:35:35.283
by giving up the name
of the doctor who does the...


01:35:35.317 --> 01:35:36.649
I can't.


01:35:38.817 --> 01:35:40.050
Why the hell not?


01:35:41.716 --> 01:35:42.884
Why not?


01:35:44.251 --> 01:35:45.283
Because...


01:35:48.117 --> 01:35:49.150
I'm the doctor.


01:35:51.083 --> 01:35:52.150
I'm the doctor.


01:35:55.117 --> 01:35:57.016
You're operating on people?


01:35:57.750 --> 01:36:00.184
It's not... It's...
It's not an operation.


01:36:00.216 --> 01:36:03.216
It's... It's a simple procedure.


01:36:03.251 --> 01:36:05.850
Joy, what are you doing?
You're operating on people?


01:36:05.884 --> 01:36:08.251
- I had to.
- How fucking stupid can you be?


01:36:08.283 --> 01:36:10.050
I had to. I...


01:36:10.083 --> 01:36:12.117
You should have stopped, Mom.
I told you that.


01:36:12.150 --> 01:36:13.417
You dragged our daughter
into this?


01:36:13.451 --> 01:36:16.150
You don't even see me.
You don't pay attention!


01:36:16.618 --> 01:36:20.850
Charlotte. Charlotte!


01:36:25.050 --> 01:36:27.750
Charlotte? Charlotte!


01:36:35.184 --> 01:36:36.649
She's at Lana's.


01:37:44.716 --> 01:37:46.050
Virginia, it's Joy.


01:37:54.484 --> 01:37:57.850
Would it be all right if...
If Charlotte stays the night?


01:37:57.884 --> 01:38:00.251
Yeah. Of course.
They're fine up there.


01:38:00.283 --> 01:38:02.150
- Thank you.
- Don't worry about it.


01:38:06.283 --> 01:38:08.117
We can talk about it
if you want.


01:38:10.417 --> 01:38:11.682
It's not...


01:38:15.184 --> 01:38:17.283
You think
you're in control of your life,


01:38:17.317 --> 01:38:18.216
and...


01:38:19.150 --> 01:38:23.083
just like that,
you realize that you're not?


01:38:33.783 --> 01:38:36.716
When Roy's boss called to
tell me about the heart attack,


01:38:41.150 --> 01:38:43.682
and that there was nothing
anyone could do...


01:38:47.451 --> 01:38:50.917
...I remember staring
at the wallpaper thinking...


01:38:53.283 --> 01:38:55.083
it just looked like
it was melting.


01:38:58.484 --> 01:39:00.817
Like the entire house
was just...


01:39:02.817 --> 01:39:04.083
falling to pieces.


01:39:06.817 --> 01:39:09.016
There's no worse feeling
in the world.


01:39:12.016 --> 01:39:13.649
So whatever you're
going through, I'm...


01:39:15.750 --> 01:39:16.716
sorry.


01:39:38.350 --> 01:39:39.949
I'm sorry. I'm...


01:39:39.984 --> 01:39:42.283
I'm so sorry.
What am I doing? I'm so sorry.


01:39:42.317 --> 01:39:43.451
No, no, no, no. I'm sorry.


01:39:43.484 --> 01:39:45.050
No, no, no.
Why... Why are you sorry?


01:39:45.083 --> 01:39:46.682
I'm the one...
I'm the one who did it.


01:39:46.716 --> 01:39:49.984
I... I don't know.
It's because I... It's what I do.


01:39:50.016 --> 01:39:51.884
I apologize.
I've always done it.


01:39:51.917 --> 01:39:53.884
I... I will always do it.


01:39:56.150 --> 01:39:57.317
Forgive me.


01:40:01.850 --> 01:40:03.016
Please.


01:40:35.016 --> 01:40:36.350
Charlotte needs you.


01:40:42.350 --> 01:40:43.783
I need you.


01:40:45.451 --> 01:40:49.417
Will... I... I need
to tell you something.


01:40:49.451 --> 01:40:51.682
No. You don't.


01:41:04.817 --> 01:41:05.750
Nixon won.


01:41:07.184 --> 01:41:07.884
He did?


01:41:08.150 --> 01:41:10.317
Mm-hmm. They called it
about an hour ago.


01:41:11.750 --> 01:41:12.949
I voted for him.


01:41:14.016 --> 01:41:15.649
Roy would have
voted for him, so...


01:41:18.451 --> 01:41:22.682
I meant to vote for Humphrey.
But I forgot.


01:41:24.817 --> 01:41:26.016
You're a Democrat?


01:41:28.016 --> 01:41:29.350
Don't tell Will.


01:41:29.384 --> 01:41:31.949
I'll break it to him gently
one day.


01:41:33.251 --> 01:41:36.216
I... I really wish
that I had been, um,


01:41:36.251 --> 01:41:39.283
helping you through this,
you know, this whole time?


01:41:40.783 --> 01:41:42.083
I don't know,


01:41:43.984 --> 01:41:46.083
with the pliers and wrenches,


01:41:46.682 --> 01:41:49.083
instead of being wrapped up
in my own...


01:41:50.484 --> 01:41:51.884
It's okay.


01:41:53.283 --> 01:41:54.384
It's okay.


01:41:56.050 --> 01:41:57.716
Thank you for saying that.


01:42:00.350 --> 01:42:02.783
But there's no need. I...


01:42:07.716 --> 01:42:09.083
Did you say pliers?


01:42:09.618 --> 01:42:13.283
Seriously?


01:42:19.283 --> 01:42:22.783
What are you doing? Huh?


01:42:28.317 --> 01:42:30.016
What I'm supposed to be doing.


01:42:30.050 --> 01:42:32.949
You know what happens to
pregnant women over time, right?


01:42:32.984 --> 01:42:34.150
They get more pregnant.


01:42:34.184 --> 01:42:37.184
Charlotte, go to Erin's, please.


01:42:37.216 --> 01:42:39.384
Why? I already know everything.


01:42:39.417 --> 01:42:41.117
The kid's right, you know?


01:42:41.150 --> 01:42:44.350
We have something that works.
We are of use.


01:42:44.884 --> 01:42:48.083
Yeah, it's not perfect,
but it works.


01:42:48.117 --> 01:42:51.317
And since you just stopped
answering your phone,


01:42:51.350 --> 01:42:53.682
I have a hundred women lined up,


01:42:53.716 --> 01:42:55.984
waiting for the doctor,
and you're it.


01:42:56.184 --> 01:42:57.850
You're all I have.


01:42:58.251 --> 01:42:59.917
You are all we have.


01:43:02.117 --> 01:43:05.184
Come on. You can't just garden


01:43:05.216 --> 01:43:07.317
and go to your PTA meetings.


01:43:08.984 --> 01:43:10.417
That's not the Joy I know.


01:43:13.083 --> 01:43:14.016
Oh, here,


01:43:14.716 --> 01:43:17.984
so you know exactly
who you are walking out on.


01:43:18.216 --> 01:43:21.216
I'm sorry about the '60s, kid.


01:43:44.150 --> 01:43:46.850
<i>Hello, is this Jane?</i>


01:43:46.884 --> 01:43:49.984
<i>I need help. Please.
I don't know what to do.</i>


01:43:55.817 --> 01:43:59.216
<i>I have 43 dollars.
This is my fourth message...</i>


01:43:59.251 --> 01:44:02.050
<i>I'm losing my grip. I thought
you were supposed to help.</i>


01:44:07.716 --> 01:44:10.817
<i>Hello? Um,
my friends gave me this number.</i>


01:44:10.850 --> 01:44:14.083
<i>I'm... I'm 15.
I'm from Riverside.</i>


01:44:14.117 --> 01:44:16.984
<i>I... I took two buses
to get to Chicago.</i>


01:44:17.016 --> 01:44:20.417
<i>I'm staying at the Travel Lodge
on Roosevelt.</i>


01:44:20.451 --> 01:44:23.083
<i>Um, room 116.</i>


01:44:23.117 --> 01:44:26.184
<i>I... I can't tell my parents.</i>


01:44:26.216 --> 01:44:28.384
<i>I'm... I'm alone here.</i>


01:44:46.451 --> 01:44:47.783
Mom?


01:44:51.417 --> 01:44:52.917
You have to go back.


01:44:57.484 --> 01:44:59.949
- Hello?
- Mm-hmm. Got it.


01:44:59.984 --> 01:45:03.283
I found this one guy
who can do 800 dollars,


01:45:03.317 --> 01:45:06.317
but he has
a terrible bedside manner.


01:45:06.350 --> 01:45:09.884
- But he's never lost anyone.
- Okay, that's a start.


01:45:09.917 --> 01:45:11.350
Good work. Yep.


01:45:11.384 --> 01:45:13.451
The Baptist ministers
are running


01:45:13.484 --> 01:45:14.949
a network up in New York.


01:45:14.984 --> 01:45:17.384
I think we can send
some people north.


01:45:17.417 --> 01:45:19.184
It will cost more
with the train ticket.


01:45:19.216 --> 01:45:21.150
Wonderful.


01:45:21.583 --> 01:45:25.216
Lateral thinking.
I love it. Keep it up.


01:45:31.817 --> 01:45:35.682
You're back... with a pumpkin.


01:46:04.150 --> 01:46:05.649
I'm going to teach you.


01:46:07.050 --> 01:46:08.682
Anybody who wants to learn.


01:46:09.184 --> 01:46:10.850
And I'll stay
as long as it takes


01:46:10.884 --> 01:46:13.117
to make you as good
as anyone can be.


01:46:16.384 --> 01:46:18.216
And then I'm going
to leave you to it.


01:46:20.350 --> 01:46:24.682
I will raise as much money
as I can to keep you going,


01:46:24.716 --> 01:46:25.417
to keep you safe.


01:46:26.917 --> 01:46:28.384
Because that's what
I can do for you,


01:46:29.384 --> 01:46:33.117
in return for all
that you have done for me.


01:46:36.251 --> 01:46:37.884
And as it turns out,


01:46:37.917 --> 01:46:40.317
I know plenty
of stuffed shirts with money.


01:46:43.884 --> 01:46:44.949
Okay?


01:46:54.317 --> 01:46:55.682
Let's get to work.


01:46:57.716 --> 01:47:01.283
<i>We performed almost
12,000 procedures</i>


01:47:01.317 --> 01:47:03.216
<i>in the years before the raid.</i>


01:47:03.251 --> 01:47:05.216
<i>We didn't lose a single woman.</i>


01:47:05.251 --> 01:47:08.050
<i>Not one. Let that sink in.</i>


01:47:08.083 --> 01:47:09.949
<i>You know who made that possible?</i>


01:47:10.850 --> 01:47:13.682
<i>You... and you...</i>


01:47:14.716 --> 01:47:17.984
<i>and even you. All of you.</i>


01:47:18.618 --> 01:47:21.451
<i>But there was one of you
who was courageous enough</i>


01:47:21.484 --> 01:47:23.050
<i>to take us right off the map...</i>


01:47:24.050 --> 01:47:25.917
<i>...and show us
what we were capable of.</i>


01:47:26.484 --> 01:47:28.984
<i>Who knew that we could
get this done ourselves?</i>


01:47:29.850 --> 01:47:30.884
<i>And we did.</i>


01:47:31.716 --> 01:47:34.283
<i>And yeah, she also bailed us out</i>


01:47:34.317 --> 01:47:37.117
<i>and never gave up the fight
to clear our names.</i>


01:47:37.716 --> 01:47:39.884
<i>And yeah,
she happens to be married</i>


01:47:39.917 --> 01:47:41.817
<i>to one hell of a criminal lawyer</i>


01:47:41.850 --> 01:47:43.283
<i>who got us out of hot water</i>


01:47:43.317 --> 01:47:45.682
<i>and helps her smooth talk</i>


01:47:45.716 --> 01:47:47.417
<i>a lot of old capitalist bastards</i>


01:47:47.451 --> 01:47:49.384
<i>into parting with their cash.</i>


01:47:52.783 --> 01:47:54.251
<i>And I think he'd tell you</i>


01:47:54.283 --> 01:47:55.850
<i>the same thing I'm telling you.</i>


01:47:57.783 --> 01:47:59.984
<i>He's lucky to have
Joy Griffin by his side.</i>


01:48:01.451 --> 01:48:02.817
<i>And so are we.</i>


01:48:04.317 --> 01:48:05.518
<i>And you know what?</i>


01:48:05.551 --> 01:48:09.884
Thank God for those seven men
on the Supreme Court, right?


01:48:12.451 --> 01:48:16.016
The other two? Fuck 'em.


01:48:16.050 --> 01:48:19.251
God, did I ever think
I would publicly thank


01:48:19.283 --> 01:48:22.117
seven men for anything?


01:48:22.984 --> 01:48:25.283
Anyway, we did it all


01:48:25.317 --> 01:48:27.150
because you showed us we could.


01:48:28.451 --> 01:48:32.016
You know, this is a...
a strange occasion.


01:48:32.783 --> 01:48:36.016
We are shutting down
because we're redundant.


01:48:36.451 --> 01:48:38.283
And I could not be happier.


01:48:39.016 --> 01:48:41.184
So...


01:48:41.216 --> 01:48:42.783
this is goodbye.


01:48:42.817 --> 01:48:47.016
But also, I hope hello...


01:48:47.050 --> 01:48:49.184
to new battles, right?


01:48:50.283 --> 01:48:53.451
And now I would
very much like you to


01:48:53.484 --> 01:48:55.150
burn the first card, kiddo.


01:48:58.117 --> 01:48:59.283
I'd be honored.


01:49:03.317 --> 01:49:05.251
Geraldine T., 15.


01:49:12.050 --> 01:49:14.750
Sally, LMP eight weeks.


01:49:17.716 --> 01:49:21.117
- So, what's next on our list?
- Oh.


01:49:21.150 --> 01:49:23.817
Pay parity? The ERA?


01:49:25.317 --> 01:49:28.016
Equal pay.


01:49:28.050 --> 01:49:29.884
Piece of cake after this, right?


01:49:29.917 --> 01:49:30.682
It's gonna be.


01:49:31.016 --> 01:49:33.117
I mean, nothing could be harder
than this, right?


01:49:33.150 --> 01:49:34.884
Right?


01:49:34.917 --> 01:49:36.251
Let's go make some trouble.


01:49:36.283 --> 01:49:37.817
You got it, Jackie O.


01:49:42.150 --> 01:49:43.649
Leticia, 14.


01:49:44.150 --> 01:49:47.050
<i>Kate, 30.
LMP eight weeks.</i>


01:49:47.083 --> 01:49:49.884
<i>Sally Anne, age 25.
LMP four weeks.</i>


01:49:49.917 --> 01:49:52.184
<i>Age 19. LMP nine weeks.</i>


01:49:52.216 --> 01:49:56.150
<i>Allison, 29.
LMP six months critical.</i>

